@DHowett @zadjii-msft To move this feature forward, I removed the WinRT dependency and added custom implementation of base64 decoding that conforms to [standard base64](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4648#section-4) with padding properly (for completeness, encoding is also added). The main idea was borrowed from [tmux base64 implementation](https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/master/compat/base64.c).

In the future, if we prefer a Windows API for base64, then we can replace in no time.

Please have a review. Thanks!

review_comments:
I supposed @DHowett is right, and we could save ourselves a bit of work with a 
```c++
if (_pfnFlushToTerminal != nullptr)
{
    return false;
}
```

here. That _should_ cause conpty to pass this through without decoding it once first. That being said, I'm pretty sure _setting the clipboard_ isn't something that's going to be done in a tight loop or end up as any sort of hot path, so I wouldn't block this PR on account of that.
